OL,3,GNEWSARail disaster of 1957 marked by St
OL,4,AJohn's plaque
OL,5,
OL,6,FA memorial plaque has been installed at
OL,7,FSt John's station in south-east London
OL,8,Fis to mark the deaths of 90 people in
OL,9,Fone of the worst disasters in British
OL,10,Frailway history.
OL,12,FMany more were also injured in the
OL,13,Fcrash - which was between Lewisham and
OL,14,FNew Cross - on 4 December 1957.
OL,16,FThis is the first memorial in St John's
OL,17,Fto honour those who were caught up in
OL,18,Fthe accident, in which two crowded
OL,19,Ftrains - one electric, one steam -
OL,20,Fcrashed on a foggy winter's evening.
OL,23,APub: 19-SepQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
